course: dictionary
lesson: 5982
title: Who is the mayor?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A mayor is the leader of a town or city council. The council looks after local things like roads, parks and rubbish. «A mayor leads a town or city.» The word leads is a clue: the mayor is in charge, a bit like the captain of a team.
explain: Some mayors have a mostly ceremonial job. In stories, a mayor opens the fair, cuts the ribbon and gives speeches. Here the words around mayor show you what the job looks like.
explain: Check a new meaning by putting it into the sentence. «Mayors, governors and premiers are chosen in elections or by elected bodies.» So a mayor is chosen by people voting. Swap in "the leader is chosen by voters" and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A mayor is the leader of a town or city council.
fact: The council takes care of things like roads, parks and rubbish.
fact: The Lord Mayor (UK) is the mayor of some big cities, and the job is often ceremonial.
fact: «Mayor» can also be a surname: Michel Mayor, with Didier Queloz, found 51 Pegasi b in 1995, the first planet known around a Sun-like star.
fact: In French, «le maire» means mayor, but it sounds like «la mère» (mother) and «la mer» (sea), so always check the spelling and the meaning.
exercise: «A mayor leads a town or city.» Who leads a town or city council? | A teacher | *A mayor | A park keeper
exercise: «Mayors, governors and premiers are chosen in elections or by elected bodies.» How is a mayor usually chosen? | *By an election | By drawing names out of a hat | A teacher picks them
exercise: Zara reads the headline «MAYOR'S SHOCKING SECRET!» What is the joke? | The mayor is a robot | The mayor has run away to sea | *The shocking secret is that he likes pineapple on pizza
test: «The mayor opened the fair and cut the ribbon.» What is the mayor doing here? | Baking bread for the fair | Ringing the school bell | *Opening the fair in a ceremony
test: Which sentence shows that Mayor can be a name, not a job? | Zara read the headline in the paper. | The mayor cut the ribbon at the fair. | *Michel Mayor found a new planet in 1995.
exam: What does mayor mean? | A planet found around a star | A king who rules the whole country | *The leader of a town or city council | A teacher who runs a school
